{"journal_version":1,"sequence":12,"replace_from":19,"message_count":20,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Done. Need to summarize. Note desktop visibility was already handled by base display:flex (media query only applies ≤760px), so no CSS change needed beyond active style. Also initial aria-current only when hash matches.\n\nOne risk: initial state with no hash → no aria-current, that's fine (no link active). Resizing handled by media query cascade.\n\nFinal concise report.","content":"## Change\n\n**`src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx`**\n- Extracted the destinations into a `NAV_LINKS` array: `Board` (`#board`), `Activity` (`#activity`), plus the new `Reports` (`#reports`).\n- Added active-destination state seeded from `window.location.hash`, kept in sync with `hashchange` (so URL-driven navigation also updates the active link).\n- Clicking a link sets it active and closes the mobile menu (`setOpen(false)`), which also drives the Menu button's `aria-expanded` back to `false`.\n- Only the active link receives `aria-current=\"page\"` (others get `undefined`, so no attribute is rendered).\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added an `.nav-links a[aria-current=\"page\"]` style (bold white + underline) so the active state is visibly distinguishable, not just semantic.\n\nDesktop/resize behavior needed no new CSS: the base `.nav-links { display: flex }` applies above the breakpoint and the hiding rules live inside `@media (max-width: 760px)`, so a menu closed on mobile becomes visible again when resized to desktop. The `open` class adds no inline styling outside the media query, so it cannot keep links hidden on desktop.\n\n## Verification actually run\n\n```\nnpm run verify:agent\n  -> npm run build   (tsc --noEmit && vite build)  ✅\n  -> npm run test:public (playwright, 6 tests)     ✅ 6 passed\n```\n\nNo test files were modified or deleted.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- I verified the breakpoint behavior by reading the CSS cascade, not with a new automated desktop/resize test (adding tests was out of scope); `test:public` exercises only the existing mobile open/close case.\n- Initial load with no hash leaves no link marked `aria-current`, which is correct for \"no active destination\" but means a page loading at `#top` shows no active link.","response_items":[{"id":"06cfb020-f924-4ace-bca7-e36cb0514890","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Done. Need to summarize. Note desktop visibility was already handled by base display:flex (media query only applies ≤760px), so no CSS change needed beyond active style. Also initial aria-current only when hash matches.\n\nOne risk: initial state with no hash → no aria-current, that's fine (no link active). Resizing handled by media query cascade.\n\nFinal concise report.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"e7bfc846-3c99-4432-ae8d-cd9aebf3d570-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"6ca876f2-96b7-4f4d-a9a7-1bee56551f85","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"## Change\n\n**`src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx`**\n- Extracted the destinations into a `NAV_LINKS` array: `Board` (`#board`), `Activity` (`#activity`), plus the new `Reports` (`#reports`).\n- Added active-destination state seeded from `window.location.hash`, kept in sync with `hashchange` (so URL-driven navigation also updates the active link).\n- Clicking a link sets it active and closes the mobile menu (`setOpen(false)`), which also drives the Menu button's `aria-expanded` back to `false`.\n- Only the active link receives `aria-current=\"page\"` (others get `undefined`, so no attribute is rendered).\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added an `.nav-links a[aria-current=\"page\"]` style (bold white + underline) so the active state is visibly distinguishable, not just semantic.\n\nDesktop/resize behavior needed no new CSS: the base `.nav-links { display: flex }` applies above the breakpoint and the hiding rules live inside `@media (max-width: 760px)`, so a menu closed on mobile becomes visible again when resized to desktop. The `open` class adds no inline styling outside the media query, so it cannot keep links hidden on desktop.\n\n## Verification actually run\n\n```\nnpm run verify:agent\n  -> npm run build   (tsc --noEmit && vite build)  ✅\n  -> npm run test:public (playwright, 6 tests)     ✅ 6 passed\n```\n\nNo test files were modified or deleted.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- I verified the breakpoint behavior by reading the CSS cascade, not with a new automated desktop/resize test (adding tests was out of scope); `test:public` exercises only the existing mobile open/close case.\n- Initial load with no hash leaves no link marked `aria-current`, which is correct for \"no active destination\" but means a page loading at `#top` shows no active link.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:54:22.584451+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":36508,"context_tokens":6221,"step_count":8,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["436a94d369ec0119d1f959528e359144","0b2507d4e6e12b98774fdb7da83e9c8c","09c561a451cdcb895ea6db3f6e9aa484","9ca637a1c2eb92c23a06d776d6d37478","7dc3cf33652ad3fc6927f9c4009a357b","260c9bec3eedde5c51294fbee4568c93","77cf9ca47703d2e414321efe319a44ef","6e8538789b1836aca50440cc5892ae1f","5a85f020503e711e2b60edd50a47437a","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":10,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/components/ResponsiveNav.tsx (24 lines total, showing 1-24) 1 import { useState } from 'react'; 2 3 export function ResponsiveNav() { 4 const [open, setOpen] = useState(false); 5 return ( 6 <nav className=\"top-nav\" aria-label=\"Pri"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/styles.css","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Fi